😷 Face Mask Detection — AI Edge Project

A lightweight deep learning project for real-time face mask detection using TensorFlow/Keras, optimized for deployment on edge devices (Raspberry Pi, Jetson Nano, Android).

🔍 Project Overview

The goal of this project is to build a real-time mask/no-mask detection system:

Input: Webcam or camera feed

Output: Bounding box with label: Mask / No Mask

Edge Deployment: Converted to TensorFlow Lite (TFLite) for low-resource devices

This project demonstrates AI-on-the-edge with real-time inference using a lightweight CNN model.

📁 Dataset

The project uses the Face Mask Detection Dataset from Kaggle:
Dataset Link

Folder structure after extraction:

face_mask_dataset/
    ├── with_mask/
    ├── without_mask/

🧠 Model Architecture
CNN Model (Edge-Friendly)

Conv2D + MaxPooling layers

Flatten → Dense → Output layer (sigmoid)

Lightweight for real-time inference

Optional Advanced Models for Research/Comparison:

MobileNetV2 or EfficientNet-lite

TFLite quantization for faster edge inference
